SUMMARY:Rice Pinnacle Lollipop: 5.3 mi.\, 530 ft. Elev. Gain
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**[Sign-up opens 8:00 PM\, Sunday 
 May 24th]**\n\n**Please read the carpool info below the hike description.*
 *\n\nThis is a typical lovely hike in the Bent Creek area. It incorporates
  segments from the Wolf Branch and Corvair Trails\, along with several con
 nectors. At 5.3 miles and a tame 530' elevation gain\, I'd rate it 2.5 on 
 a 0-10 difficulty scale. We'll average around 2.4 mph -- not a fitness hik
 e\, but you should have enough experience hiking to know you can deal with
  mild hills and a moderate pace.\n\nWe'll stop for a brief snack & water b
 reak halfway around. Wear sensible hiking boots. If you're on the fence ab
 out hiking poles\, you probably don't need them for this one.\n\n***Dog Po
 licy:*** Dogs are extremely welcome but must be leashed.\n\n***Guest Polic
 y:*** If you'd like to bring a guest\, they should join the Asheville Hiki
 ng Group and sign up for the hike on their own. Alternatively\, contact me
  in advance and ask if it's okay to bring a "+1" after you've made it onto
  the "Going" list. Depending on timing and demand\, I MAY be able to add y
 our guest.\n\n**MEET-UP TIME AND PLACE**\nOptional carpooling on this hike
 \, but it's encouraged. We'll rendezvous at the **Asheville Outlets parkin
 g lot\, just behind the Waffle House on Brevard Rd. (Rt. 191)**. We'll hea
 d over to the Rice Pinnacle parking lot at 8:45 am.\n\nIf you're parking a
 t the trailhead\, please come a few minutes early for check-in and intros.
  Look for me at my silver Hyundai. We'll hit the trail a.s.a.p. after 9:00
  AM.\n\n**DIRECTIONS TO TRAILHEAD**\n\n* From Exit 33 on I-26\,\n* Head so
 uth on Brevard Rd. (Rt. 191) for 2 miles\n* Right at the lights on Bent Cr
 eek Ranch Rd.\n* After .3 miles bear left onto Wesley Branch Rd.\n* Go abo
 ut 1.4 miles and turn right just past the sign for the Rice Pinnacle Trail
 head\n* Go left at the fork. You'll see the parking lot after a short dist
 ance.\n\n**Click here for the location on [Google Maps](https://maps.app.g
 oo.gl/totfTN3YMWYcU9KE7)**\n\n**COURTESY TO WAIT-LISTERS (Please abide!)**
 \nOnly sign up if you \\*TRULY\\* plan to come. If you must cancel\, pleas
 e change your status to "Not Going" as soon as possible so wait-listers wi
 ll have sufficient notice. And please please PLEASE don't be a no-show.\n\
 nIf you're on the waiting list\, keep checking the evening before. Despite
  what I wrote above\, we always get last-minute dropouts.\n\n**WEATHER**\n
 I'll monitor National Weather Service forecasts for the hike area and emai
 l cancellation messages by 7:30 AM if the forecast is for more than a 50% 
 chance of precipitation.\n\n**QUESTIONS?**\nIf you have any questions\, me
 ssage me through MeetUp until 8:30 AM the day of. Cell reception may be sk
 etchy\, but you can try to text or call me up to the start of the hike: (8
 03) 767-3094.\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-
 \\-\n\n**LEGALESE**\n\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking a
 nd\, possibly\, transportation to and from the meetup site. Participants a
 re responsible for their own safety and\, by joining a hike\, affirm that 
 they have the appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, equipment\, and
  supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and property. Neither your 
 hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can eliminate all risks or be re
 sponsible for your well-being. Participants assume full responsibility for
  any injuries\, damages\, or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/314934015
 /
