SUMMARY:Bearwallow Mountain up and over\, out and back
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n[https://maps.app.goo.gl/3gcVKqRCy
 i416ULs9](https://maps.app.goo.gl/3gcVKqRCyi416ULs9)\n\napprox 5 miles\, 9
 50 feet of elevation gain\n\nthis is a beautiful trail with some moderatel
 y technical (rocky) areas. we go up and over Bearwallow mountain proper\, 
 taking a short break at the top\, then down into the valley between it and
  Little Bearwallow on the first portion of the Wildcat Rock trail. then 2n
 d break for rest\, snack and water\, then return to the trailhead\n\npace 
 of 2.0 - 2.5 mph\n\nwell behaved dogs are welcome to attend. this hike is 
 unique in that there is a resident herd of cattle\, and we don't want any 
 dog v. cow scenarios. i'm a big fan of off-leash dogs on hikes\, but a lea
 sh may be needed around the cows\n\nper previous hikes:\n\ngear up as appr
 opriate\, trekking poles are an option. bring a snack as we'll take a brea
 k mid-hike. oh and plenty of water!\n\nground rules: 1) if you sign up\, s
 how up or change your status. 2 ) be sure you are in adequate physical sha
 pe to complete the event. 3) show consideration toward all atendees. I hik
 e for stress reduction and want to keep it that way as much as possible\n\
 n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, pos
 sibly\, transportation to and from the meetup site. Participants are respo
 nsible for their own safety and affirm that they have the appropriate skil
 ls\, physical conditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve 
 risks to oneself and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville H
 iking Group can assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. By signing up 
 for this event\, participant understands and agrees
